23,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,Our yards are a mess of old gear and we can't stop for a cutover in winter. We need something rugged and flexible.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems the board prefers operating expenses over capital hits, but separate licenses are a trap. We need a bundled or outright cost.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Asuka,,We have a disaster waiting to happen. Support is fragmented and our initial project scopes are unrealistic. We need clear ownership and adaptability.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out we skip upgrades because they're too hard, and outside help left us with messy data! We can't have that again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are losing our institutional memory, and trainers are being ignored on the floor. A system that imposes itself from above will fail.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if the scope always changes, maybe a fixed configuration is a bad idea?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, if the staff is stretched, a system that requires heavy internal administration will be a liability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, exactly. A rigid process will break the moment the business shifts. We need a vendor that stays involved.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, does that mean we should avoid the ones that just give us the software and leave?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, Rin. We need a partner who understands the people, not just the process.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm worried about any ""cloud"" solution that doesn't account for our old handhelds or the peak season chaos.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I'll be wary of any modular licensing. If we buy pieces separately, the costs will spiral as we grow.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I want a single point of accountability. No more pointing fingers during an outage.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I want something that doesn't just ""age in place."" It has to be easy to keep current!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,We must prioritize a vendor that provides hands-on support and training that actually sticks with the supervisors.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
