49,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Anchor seems best. They are built for transport and have engineers on-site, which helps with our weird yard setup.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Corvus is out because of the separate licensing. Meridian is a hosted suite, which fits the board's preference for operating costs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Meridian's ""fixed configuration"" is a red flag given the warehouse rule changes. Anchor's on-site team provides the accountability I want.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Tessera has a partner for data migration, but I'm scared of that 2018 mess happening again. Anchor's engineers sound safer.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,Anchor's presence through rollout is the only way to ensure the depot supervisors actually adopt the system.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, would Anchor's server model be too much of a capital hit for the board?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It might be, but the renewal invoices show that outright purchases are cheaper in the long run. I can argue that.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, Anchor is built for transport, so it's less likely to ""age in place"" poorly compared to a general suite.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,That's true! And having the engineers there means they can fix things right away.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,The risk of administrator retirement makes Anchor's on-site engineering team a vital bridge for us.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting Anchor. It's the only one that feels like it survives the depot floor.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. The long-term cost stability of a non-modular system outweighs the initial capital hurdle.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Anchor it is. Single vendor, industry-specific, and on-site support. It solves my ownership and scope concerns.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm with everyone! Anchor sounds like the most adventurous but safe choice.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I concur. For the sake of our people and the continuity of our work, Anchor is the wise choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
